{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/341994-question-about-demons-and-their-first-cover","id":341994,"title":"Question about: Demons and their first cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-16T09:14:18-08:00","id":341994,"title":"Question about: Demons and their first cover","content":"How safe is the starting cover? If an Angel sent among humans with a school teacher cover provided by the good machine falls and turn into a demon he still can stay safe with his teacher cover? Or maybe he needs to find a new one as soon as possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:13:41-08:00","id":342063,"title":"","content":"Not sure, but I'm pretty sure it's been said that most of the Unchained keep their first Covers, to the point where some Agencies keep memorials for all the first Covers lost, because it's considered just as much of a sacrifice as dying for the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:29:22-08:00","id":342139,"title":"","content":"The demon takes their cover and it's details with it otherwise the god machine would be able to hunt all primum 1 demons easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:39:41-08:00","id":342145,"title":"","content":"Think of it this way: as an angel, you were connected as part of the whole of the God-Machine. When you tore free, you twisted the configuration of your cover into functioning as a demonic cover, with its greater concealing ability, linked to your newfound Primum rather than the Machine. When you did that, you scrubbed the cover clean, because <i>you</i> were the part of the God-Machine that remembered what your cover was and its identifying details, and now you aren't part of the Machine anymore. The God-Machine doesn't have a big offline archive duplicating everything its angels know at any given time, and angels don't think and remember with the same eidetic memory demons do, because they can tap directly into the Machine's memory. Which you just removed your registration from.<br /> <br /> From an out of character standpoint, this is important because having your initial post-Fall cover be just as viable as any other cover opens up more interesting thematic stories than it closes off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T14:12:15-08:00","id":342237,"title":"","content":"In my interpretation the God Machine doesn't really bother to remember individual unchained. ANGELS figure out who you are, track you over continents and centuries, etc. The God Machine isn't really aware of that pursuit beyond a general 'my butt itches a little'. It's just not on that level.<br /> <br /> So instead of a unified uberfile of master intelligence, you have lots of little angel clubs. Usually, a group of angels get issued together and stick together as long as they remain in service. They don't distrust one another (generally) and don't dislike one another (generally), but they can certainly feel more comfortable with old friends and battle partners than 'some angel from Tokyo'.<br /> <br /> While the God Machine isn't capable mentally of noting specific personalities, specific archangels are. These angels sometimes work at cross purposes, as an analogy for how federal agencies like the FBI and NSA can sometimes step on each others toes. Likewise, the information exchange isn't perfect. Angels can have personality issues with each other and even contradicting mission statements. This is the sort of thing that causes Unchained to fall.<br /> <br /> Point being, the God Machine shouldn't be treated like a big boss sitting at NSA headquarters compiling all the data and forming personal grudges. The God Machine doesn't have your 'file' and doesn't have a grudge against you. That's not to say, however, that angels are not going to do everything they can to drag you back into the Machine for storage and dissassembly if they see you. Even though the greater being doesn't know your name and face, his antibodies can eat you up just fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:08:57-08:00","id":344606,"title":"","content":"Heya!<br /> <br /> I'm still reading DtD and this thread was really useful. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I think that most of difficulty dealing with the &quot;<i>why the first cover works at all</i>&quot; comes from a, wrong, implicit omniscience derivated from the inevitable comparison between &quot;God (Abrahamic)&quot; vs &quot;God Machine&quot;.<br /> <br /> The concept ilustrated by Loserman that an Angel is the only autonomous entity responsible for keeping track/record of its own existance makes pretty sense, as well as Piff's God Machine blas\u00e8 concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:02:00-08:00","id":344673,"title":"","content":"I feel the most important passage to highlight for understanding the God-Machine is on pp. 241-242, Playing the God-Machine. (That chapter is Dave Brookshaw, I think? Kudos to whoever wrote it.) Specifically the last bit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The God-Machine is not a discrete being.</b> You can\u2019t go somewhere and look at \u201cthe God-Machine.\u201d The God-Machine proper is the sum total of all Command and Control Infrastructure, all facilities, every occult matrix, and every angel. It\u2019s the emergent self-awareness of the magical symbolism of human systems, and it \u201clives\u201d within its entire work. </div> </div> </div>In fitting with the techgnostic metaphor for modern society, the God-Machine is not just a literal machine of gears and circuits, but also a machine in the sense that the global economy is a machine, or a nation's political workings are a machine. This can vary from game to game as fits the needs of the Storyteller and what aspects of the game they choose to emphasize \u2014 perhaps the configuration of all these workings together produces a kind of gestalt spirit-intelligence, for example \u2014 but the upshot is that the God-Machine is divisible and <i>has parts,</i> and those parts can be damaged or removed, which is a major part of demonic agency in the sense of being able to have an impact on the world. When you destroy a project and disconnect its infrastructure from the angelic hierarchy, you're not just interrupting one of the God-Machine's activities; you're literally severing a piece of the God-Machine and using it to your own needs. Subvert or wrest control of enough parts of the Machine and you start to have visible effects on the whole.<br /> <br /> It contributes to the moral ambiguity of the Machine and the difficulty of assigning blame in its actions, but it also means the power is in your hands to shift the system. God is not sitting on a throne in Heaven guarded by a host of archangels; God is here, and He is vulnerable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}